## Part III — Derived Data Products (CC0 1.0 Universal)

The derived tabular and spatiotemporal data products created by this project
are released under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal public-domain
dedication (**CC0 1.0 Universal**). This includes, without limitation:

- `submission.csv` and its documented schema;
- the derived tables under `data/processed/*`; and
- the derived monthly, annual, and gridded summaries produced by the project
  pipeline from the source observations.

These products are built from public-domain NASA LANCE FIRMS / Earthdata
active-fire observations and Natural Earth public-domain boundaries. NASA
data are provided under the NASA Open Data Policy (CC0 / 17 U.S.C. § 105);
Natural Earth data are public domain (CC0).

To the extent possible under law, the Fire Relay South America Contributors
have waived all copyright and related or neighboring rights to these derived
data products. You may copy, modify, distribute, and use the products for any
purpose without asking permission. The full legal code is available at
<https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode>. A
human-readable summary is available at
<https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>.

The CC0 dedication applies only to the derived products created by this
project. It does not alter the terms of the upstream NASA, Earthdata, Natural
Earth, or other third-party sources, and it does not grant rights in the
underlying observations beyond those provided by the source terms.

